Quick DevOps Tip: NGINX – Reload vs Restart 🔄

Ever wondered what the actual difference is between:

sudo service nginx reload vs sudo service nginx restart

They may look similar, but the impact they have on your web server is very different 👇

🔁 reload = Graceful reload

Applies changes to your NGINX config (nginx.conf)
Keeps current connections alive
Spins up new workers with the updated config
Old workers finish their tasks before exiting

🛑 restart = Full stop & start

Shuts down all processes immediately
Drops all ongoing connections
Starts the service from scratch

🔧 Best practice:

Use reload when you tweak configs and want zero downtime
Use restart when things go wrong or you make deeper changes

✅ Always test your NGINX config before a reload/restart:
sudo nginx -t
